# Office / portal auth

Authentication and authorization are separate.

- Staff: Microsoft Entra workforce + SWA Easy Auth (`aad`). Renters are never B2B guests in this tenant.
- Renters: Microsoft Entra External ID (separate customer tenant) + Google/Apple/Microsoft/email. SWA provider id `externalid`.
- Sign-in is not permission to act. Office APIs re-check `permissionGate()` against the catalog. Portal APIs scope every query to the signed-in person's email.
- Keep workforce enterprise-app **Assignment required** off so login is not blocked with `AADSTS50105`.
- Public exceptions (contact, apply, Stripe webhook) use Turnstile / Stripe signatures — not office login.
- Local Functions (`AZURE_FUNCTIONS_ENVIRONMENT=Development`) grant the full office catalog so `func start` works without SWA headers.

See `docs/architecture/authentication-authorization.md`.
